# Database conventions

Drizzle ORM over Neon Postgres. App schema lives in `src/schema.ts` (re-exports
`auth-schema.ts` for Better Auth tables). Domain query functions live in one
file per table and are re-exported from `src/index.ts`.

## Schema

camelCase in TypeScript, snake_case in the column name. App-owned tables get
`id` (uuid), `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `deletedAt`, all timestamps
`withTimezone: true`.

Better Auth tables in `src/auth-schema.ts` are library-owned. They use `text`
ids and do not follow the soft-delete convention.

```ts
export const user = pgTable("user", {
  id: text("id").primaryKey(),
  email: text("email").notNull().unique(),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow().notNull(),
});

export type User = typeof user.$inferSelect;
export type NewUser = typeof user.$inferInsert;
```

Always export the inferred `$inferSelect` and `$inferInsert` types next to the
table. Never hand-write a row type.

## Soft delete

For app-owned tables, deletes are soft: set `deletedAt`, never `db.delete()`.
Every read filters it out.

```ts
.where(and(eq(tasks.userId, userId), isNull(tasks.deletedAt)))
```

## Query functions

Plain exported functions taking `db: Db` as the first argument, with an explicit
return type. No classes, no repository objects. Inputs get a named
`<Verb><Thing>Input` type.

```ts
export async function findTaskById(
  db: Db,
  taskId: string,
): Promise<Task | undefined> {
  const rows = await db.select().from(tasks).where(...).limit(1);
  return rows[0];
}
```

Use `.limit(1)` and return `rows[0]` for single lookups. Use `.returning()` on
insert and update.

## Migrations

Run `pnpm db:generate` after any schema edit and commit the generated SQL in
`packages/db/drizzle`. Never edit a generated migration by hand.
